data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Per token: $\\rho = \\exp(\\text{logp\\_new} - \\text{logp\\_old})$. The surrogate is the minimum of\n$\\rho A$ and $\\operatorname{clip}(\\rho, 1-\\varepsilon, 1+\\varepsilon) A$, with $A$ taken from the\nresponse. The $k_3$ term uses $\\delta = \\text{logp\\_ref} - \\text{logp\\_new}$ and equals $e^{\\delta} - \\delta - 1$.\nAverage the masked per-token losses within each response, then across responses."},"hints_note":null}

